# Analytics on thequietachievr.com

When adding or changing **links, buttons, forms, or conversion CTAs**, ensure they are tracked in **PostHog** and **Google Analytics** (providers in `src/app/layout.tsx`).

## Default behavior

`PostHogProvider` and `GoogleAnalyticsProvider` already capture:

- `$pageview` / page views on route change
- `ui_click` on `<a>`, `<button>`, and `[role="button"]` clicks (label, href, path)

That is not enough for **product analytics**. Add explicit events for CTAs that matter (book buy, coaching, newsletter, downloads, conversions).

## Custom events — PostHog

Import posthog in client components:

```tsx
import posthog from "posthog-js";

if (posthog.__loaded) {
  posthog.capture("event_name_snake_case", {
    label: "...",
    href: "...",
    path: window.location.pathname,
  });
}
```

Follow existing names where possible: `ui_click`, `chapter_download_signup`, `playbook_access_granted`, `conversion_completed`, `bio_link_arrival`, `bio_link_touch`.

## Custom events — Google Analytics

Use the same pattern as `google-analytics-provider.tsx`:

```tsx
sendEvent("event_name_snake_case", { ...params });
```

Or rely on `ui_click` if the global handler is sufficient for a simple nav link.

## Bio-link attribution

Pages that receive traffic from `links.thequietachievr.com` should preserve:

- URL params: `tqa_phid`, `utm_*`
- Cookie: `tqa_attribution` (read via `src/lib/bio-attribution.ts`)

Conversion pages (e.g. `/book/thank-you`) use `ConversionTracker` — add similar components for new funnel endpoints.

## New outbound or buy links

Append UTMs / `tqa_phid` when linking from owned surfaces, or document why not. Book/coaching CTAs should remain measurable in PostHog funnels.

## Checklist before finishing

- [ ] Meaningful CTAs have an explicit PostHog event (not only autocapture)
- [ ] GA receives the same or equivalent event when GA is connected
- [ ] Conversion flows fire a dedicated event (e.g. `conversion_completed`, form success)
- [ ] No raw email or secrets in analytics payloads
